es. For more information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion during the afternoons and evenings both\nWednesday and Thursday.","ends":"2026-08-27T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Weld, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Larimer, CO; Broomfield, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-27T00:16:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 270016 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 616 PM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered afternoon/evening thunderstorms expected for theI-25 Corridor and plains. A few storms could become severe, with large hail and strong winds possible. - Thunderstorm coverage decreases Thursday and Friday with mainly isolated high-based showers/s","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T20:23:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Thursday...Scattered thunderstorms will move across the urban corridor and eastern plains late this afternoon and early evening with heavy rain, hail, and strong winds. Warmer and drier air moves in for Thursday with isolated high-based showers/thunderstorms. Gusty outflow winds will accompany the showers/thunderstorms while any rainfall will be light. LONG TERM","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU